1
00:00:06,447 --> 00:00:08,117
(Space Rice Cake)

2
00:00:08,757 --> 00:00:10,957
(Space Rice Cake)

3
00:00:11,357 --> 00:00:15,257
(After a long, hard struggle with rice cakes, )

4
00:00:15,597 --> 00:00:20,127
(the place grew into a decent restaurant.)

5
00:00:21,697 --> 00:00:24,207
(And they finally opened the restaurant.)

6
00:00:25,207 --> 00:00:28,477
(But the streets were empty.)

7
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:30,607
(She's posing for photos here.)

8
00:00:30,807 --> 00:00:32,476
(But we're taking a break right now.)

9
00:00:32,477 --> 00:00:34,293
(We're not taking a break. We're open for business!)

10
00:00:34,317 --> 00:00:37,017
(With the labour-management conflict escalating, )

11
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:40,387
(the owner backed down and chose the carrot over the stick.)

12
00:00:40,757 --> 00:00:43,457
(They joined forces again, )

13
00:00:43,827 --> 00:00:46,457
(and Space Rice Cake has no empty tables left now.)

14
00:00:46,957 --> 00:00:49,927
(Meanwhile, some people are approaching the restaurant.)

15
00:00:50,627 --> 00:00:52,197
- Oh, my. Hello.
- Hello.

16
00:00:52,527 --> 00:00:53,897
Welcome.

17
00:00:54,237 --> 00:00:55,767
- How many in your party?
- Two.

18
00:00:55,867 --> 00:00:57,207
- Two?
- Hello.

19
00:00:57,437 --> 00:00:58,866
Welcome to our restaurant. But I'm sorry.

20
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:00,137
- We're currently...
- Yes?

21
00:01:00,377 --> 00:01:01,877
- completely full.
- I see.

22
00:01:02,277 --> 00:01:05,376
May I put you on the waitlist using this application?

23
00:01:05,377 --> 00:01:06,507
- Sure.
- Okay. Got it.

24
00:01:07,517 --> 00:01:08,916
Thank you so much.

25
00:01:08,917 --> 00:01:10,046
- If you could wait just a bit, - Yes.

26
00:01:10,047 --> 00:01:12,547
We'll contact you as soon as your table is ready.

27
00:01:12,887 --> 00:01:15,256
We have people on the waitlist.

28
00:01:15,257 --> 00:01:16,257
Do we?

29
00:01:16,258 --> 00:01:17,898
- We have one party on the list.
- I see.

30
00:01:18,187 --> 00:01:21,457
I'm not really used to being this famous.

31
00:01:21,897 --> 00:01:23,226
What is going on?

32
00:01:23,227 --> 00:01:24,766
This is way beyond our expectations.

33
00:01:24,767 --> 00:01:26,447
- Yu Jin, did you tell them?
- Yes, I did.

34
00:01:26,727 --> 00:01:27,766
- We have customers on the waitlist.
- Customers on the waitlist.

35
00:01:27,767 --> 00:01:28,866
- The first party on our waitlist.
- Customers on the waitlist.

36
00:01:28,867 --> 00:01:30,343
- Thank you. I owe it to you.
- You're welcome.

37
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:32,066
- Honesty, humility.
- Humility.

38
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:33,337
- Ahk.
- Ahk.

39
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:35,377
(Screaming)

40
00:01:35,577 --> 00:01:37,006
- Chef Kim Mi Hyun.
- Yes?

41
00:01:37,007 --> 00:01:38,777
- Are you tired?
- I'm crazy.

42
00:01:39,277 --> 00:01:40,277
- That's not what she asked.
- Sorry?

43
00:01:40,278 --> 00:01:41,346
- She asked if you were tired.
- I asked if you were tired.

44
00:01:41,347 --> 00:01:42,947
I'm crazy.

45
00:01:43,887 --> 00:01:46,016
- How's everything going now?
- It's going well.

46
00:01:46,017 --> 00:01:47,057
Is it?

47
00:01:47,187 --> 00:01:49,787
- Have you closed out any tables?
- No, I haven't.

48
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:52,126
Can you check...

49
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:54,497
how the customers like original tteokbokki?

50
00:01:54,827 --> 00:01:56,796
- How's everything going out there?
- They all love it.

51
00:01:56,797 --> 00:01:57,943
- Is everything going well?
- Yes.

52
00:01:57,967 --> 00:01:59,596
Do our customers seem happy with our food?

53
00:01:59,597 --> 00:02:00,697
- Of course.
- Absolutely.

54
00:02:00,767 --> 00:02:02,207
- Are they enjoying the food?
- Yes.

55
00:02:02,667 --> 00:02:03,866
What did they say?

56
00:02:03,867 --> 00:02:05,206
(Chef Young Ji, the anxious type)

57
00:02:05,207 --> 00:02:06,766
Young Ji, they all really like your food.

58
00:02:06,767 --> 00:02:08,036
- Really? Do they like it?
- Yes.

59
00:02:08,037 --> 00:02:09,576
- You mean, original tteokbokki?
- Everything.

60
00:02:09,577 --> 00:02:10,876
- Really? Thank you.
- Yes.

61
00:02:10,877 --> 00:02:12,607
They all love your tteokbokki.

62
00:02:12,877 --> 00:02:14,347
Really? I'm relieved.

63
00:02:15,117 --> 00:02:17,146
Eun Ji has worked...

64
00:02:17,147 --> 00:02:18,847
- all kinds of jobs.
- That's right.

65
00:02:19,187 --> 00:02:21,187
She's a perfect and sexy career woman.

66
00:02:21,917 --> 00:02:24,157
Thank you, Village Chief. I can tell...

67
00:02:24,657 --> 00:02:26,357
you really got the word out.

68
00:02:26,687 --> 00:02:28,397
We have some customers waiting outside.

69
00:02:28,657 --> 00:02:29,657
- Really?
- Yes.

70
00:02:29,658 --> 00:02:31,027
They're on our waitlist.

71
00:02:31,127 --> 00:02:32,127
Thank you.

72
00:02:32,627 --> 00:02:34,096
Thank you.

73
00:02:34,097 --> 00:02:35,296
Thank you, everyone.

74
00:02:35,297 --> 00:02:37,206
- Yes, ma'am.
- I'm your first customer.

75
00:02:37,207 --> 00:02:38,536
- That's right, ma'am.
- I wish you great success.

76
00:02:38,537 --> 00:02:39,836
Thank you, ma'am.

77
00:02:39,837 --> 00:02:41,336
- I really enjoyed the food.
- Thank you.

78
00:02:41,337 --> 00:02:43,383
- May you all be blessed.
- You too. Get home safely.

79
00:02:43,407 --> 00:02:45,967
(The head of the women's association is getting ready to leave.)

80
00:02:46,047 --> 00:02:48,316
Take your time and enjoy the food. We're off now.

81
00:02:48,317 --> 00:02:50,717
Won't you take him with you?

82
00:02:51,147 --> 00:02:53,086
Don't you have somewhere to be, Reverend?

83
00:02:53,087 --> 00:02:54,756
- How much do I owe you?
- It's 12 dollars.

84
00:02:54,757 --> 00:02:56,157
- Twelve dollars?
- Yes.

85
00:02:56,617 --> 00:02:58,617
(Maybe he's sad to leave, so he chugs his slushy.)

86
00:02:58,727 --> 00:03:00,526
- Are you leaving, sir?
- Yes.

87
00:03:00,527 --> 00:03:01,657
Thank you for coming.

88
00:03:01,827 --> 00:03:03,967
- Thank you.
- Get home safely.

89
00:03:04,727 --> 00:03:06,596
Hello. I'm calling from Space Rice Cake.

90
00:03:06,597 --> 00:03:07,796
(Eun Ji calls the waiting customer right away.)

91
00:03:07,797 --> 00:03:09,867
Yes, you can come now.

92
00:03:10,237 --> 00:03:13,737
(Meanwhile, Young Ji goes to check on the hall for the first time.)

93
00:03:13,977 --> 00:03:15,377
Are you enjoying the food?

94
00:03:15,707 --> 00:03:16,707
(Thumbs up)

95
00:03:16,707 --> 00:03:17,707
- Thank you.
- It's good.

96
00:03:17,708 --> 00:03:18,976
Is tteokramisu a big portion?

97
00:03:18,977 --> 00:03:20,516
- No, the portion size isn't so big.
- Is it big enough for us to share?

98
00:03:20,517 --> 00:03:21,846
I think it's big enough for you to share.

99
00:03:21,847 --> 00:03:23,376
- It's delicious.
- Can we get pomegranate slushy too?

100
00:03:23,377 --> 00:03:25,716
- Sure. Of course.
- Thank you.

101
00:03:25,717 --> 00:03:26,887
Thank you.

102
00:03:27,317 --> 00:03:29,086
Tteokramisu cake.

103
00:03:29,087 --> 00:03:31,087
(Thrilled to receive the very first dessert order)

104
00:03:31,127 --> 00:03:34,697
Tteokramisu and pomegranate slushy.

105
00:03:35,027 --> 00:03:38,127
(She starts making the dessert right away.)

106
00:03:38,567 --> 00:03:39,966
(She cuts the coffee-soaked baekseolgi into smaller pieces.)

107
00:03:39,967 --> 00:03:41,773
(She cuts the coffee-soaked baekseolgi into smaller pieces.)

108
00:03:41,797 --> 00:03:43,836
(In a pretty dessert cup, )

109
00:03:43,837 --> 00:03:45,967
(she places the first layer.)

110
00:03:46,307 --> 00:03:48,137
(The next step is...)

111
00:03:48,607 --> 00:03:50,577
(to pipe the chestnut cream.)

112
00:03:51,377 --> 00:03:55,677
(Here comes the key ingredient she learned to make.)

113
00:03:58,287 --> 00:04:01,357
(Sticky)

114
00:04:02,287 --> 00:04:04,086
(On top of the chestnut cream, )

115
00:04:04,087 --> 00:04:05,927
(she puts real chestnuts to add some texture.)

116
00:04:06,157 --> 00:04:09,227
(She adds another layer of baekseolgi.)

117
00:04:09,897 --> 00:04:13,967
(She pipes the chestnut cream one more time.)

118
00:04:14,367 --> 00:04:16,237
(She adds more real chestnuts.)

119
00:04:16,897 --> 00:04:18,636
(Lastly, )

120
00:04:18,637 --> 00:04:21,677
(she grates some chestnuts to make chestnut powder!)

121
00:04:26,907 --> 00:04:29,277
(A big pile of chestnut powder)

122
00:04:29,847 --> 00:04:32,146
(She decorates it with an apple mint leaf...)

123
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:34,456
(and a whole chestnut to wrap up.)

124
00:04:34,457 --> 00:04:36,317
You did a wonderful job.

125
00:04:36,487 --> 00:04:37,487
(The first tteokramisu chestnut is ready.)

126
00:04:37,488 --> 00:04:40,008
- You really did a great job today.
- They're going to love it.

127
00:04:40,257 --> 00:04:43,827
(He slices smoothly through the soft tteokramisu.)

128
00:04:44,597 --> 00:04:47,027
(And he takes a big bite.)

129
00:04:48,797 --> 00:04:49,837
It's good.

130
00:04:50,167 --> 00:04:51,907
(The village chief takes a bite too.)

131
00:04:52,037 --> 00:04:53,917
- It's sweet and delicious, right?
- It's good.

132
00:04:54,507 --> 00:04:56,637
(The tteokramisu chestnut is completely devoured.)

133
00:04:57,247 --> 00:04:59,847
- Is it good?
- Yes. The food is good here.

134
00:05:00,277 --> 00:05:01,777
The chef here is very famous.

135
00:05:04,717 --> 00:05:07,257
- It's true.
- Who's this chef, Uncle?

136
00:05:08,317 --> 00:05:09,663
Her name is Lee Young Suk, I think.

137
00:05:09,687 --> 00:05:10,726
(Laughing)

138
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:11,757
Her name is Lee Young Ji.

139
00:05:11,927 --> 00:05:15,026
(Lee Young Suk, a famous chef in Goheung)

140
00:05:15,027 --> 00:05:16,057
By the way, Yu Jin.

141
00:05:16,297 --> 00:05:20,297
The dining room truly feels like a cosy parlour...

142
00:05:20,467 --> 00:05:21,896
- Yes, indeed.
- with all the seniors there.

143
00:05:21,897 --> 00:05:23,137
- It has a warm vibe.
- Yes.

144
00:05:23,967 --> 00:05:25,567
- Order's up.
- Okay.

145
00:05:25,937 --> 00:05:27,677
Small original tteokbokki,

146
00:05:28,537 --> 00:05:31,107
tteokramisu chestnut, and fancy coffee slushy.

147
00:05:31,377 --> 00:05:33,106
I'll do the dishes.

148
00:05:33,107 --> 00:05:35,877
(With no orders for her coming in, Mimi steps up to do the dishes.)

149
00:05:36,477 --> 00:05:40,217
(Young Ji starts making the small original tteokbokki.)

150
00:05:40,857 --> 00:05:41,916
(The village chief, who contributed so much to the successful opening, )

151
00:05:41,917 --> 00:05:43,563
(and his party are getting ready to leave.)

152
00:05:43,587 --> 00:05:45,627
- I can ring you up here.
- Can you get their bill?

153
00:05:46,687 --> 00:05:49,897
You had a small portion of original tteokbokki...

154
00:05:50,327 --> 00:05:52,697
And pomegranate slushy too.

155
00:05:53,397 --> 00:05:55,066
Your total comes to 45.9 dollars.

156
00:05:55,067 --> 00:05:56,613
- Are you paying with a card...
- The table...

157
00:05:56,637 --> 00:05:59,006
We'll pay for table three too.

158
00:05:59,007 --> 00:06:00,737
Shall I ring you up for table three too?

159
00:06:01,577 --> 00:06:02,677
Please give me a second.

160
00:06:03,007 --> 00:06:05,007
(She rushes to find Mi Suk's bill.)

161
00:06:06,947 --> 00:06:12,147
(But she can't tell which is hers.)

162
00:06:12,687 --> 00:06:15,817
(She steps out with both for now.)

163
00:06:16,087 --> 00:06:18,057
You had a small portion of original tteokbokki...

164
00:06:18,857 --> 00:06:20,387
and tteokramisu chestnut.

165
00:06:21,157 --> 00:06:22,296
Is that right?

166
00:06:22,297 --> 00:06:24,267
- Actually...
- We had pollack roe pasta too.

167
00:06:24,897 --> 00:06:26,066
That must be the bill for that table.

168
00:06:26,067 --> 00:06:27,797
(She got it confused with another table.)

169
00:06:28,067 --> 00:06:29,567
Right? I'm sorry.

170
00:06:30,397 --> 00:06:32,766
- Then...
- How will you survive in business?

171
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,737
I know, right? What do I do?

172
00:06:35,207 --> 00:06:36,536
(The village chief's table, total: 45.9 dollars)

173
00:06:36,537 --> 00:06:37,906
(Mi Suk's table, total: 36.9 dollars)

174
00:06:37,907 --> 00:06:39,977
(Total: 82.8 dollars)

175
00:06:40,077 --> 00:06:41,817
(That's the total amount, but...)

176
00:06:41,977 --> 00:06:43,947
Your total comes to 72.8 dollars.

177
00:06:44,647 --> 00:06:45,947
I'm sorry about that.

178
00:06:46,787 --> 00:06:48,686
(She has no idea she made a mistake at the register.)

179
00:06:48,687 --> 00:06:50,117
Thank you.

180
00:06:50,727 --> 00:06:51,756
We really enjoyed the food.

181
00:06:51,757 --> 00:06:53,656
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

182
00:06:53,657 --> 00:06:55,827
- Go home safely. Thank you.
- Thank you.

183
00:06:56,597 --> 00:06:57,597
(Sighing with relief)

184
00:06:58,397 --> 00:07:00,527
So this one was it. It was here.

185
00:07:01,637 --> 00:07:04,437
(She stares suspiciously at the bill.)

186
00:07:05,167 --> 00:07:08,337
(But she never realised she made a mistake.)

187
00:07:09,077 --> 00:07:10,846
One small original tteokbokki is up.

188
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:11,946
Got it.

189
00:07:11,947 --> 00:07:13,047
Let's do this!

190
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:14,346
All right.

191
00:07:14,347 --> 00:07:16,553
(1 small original tteokbokki, 1 tteokramisu, 1 coffee slushy)

192
00:07:16,577 --> 00:07:18,346
One small original tteokbokki is up.

193
00:07:18,347 --> 00:07:19,547
(She serves the food quickly.)

194
00:07:19,587 --> 00:07:22,316
You see, our plates are very heavy.

195
00:07:22,317 --> 00:07:24,197
(Dirty plates keep rolling in without a break.)

196
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:27,057
- Thank you, Mimi.
- Don't worry about it.

197
00:07:27,157 --> 00:07:28,256
Thank you so much.

198
00:07:28,257 --> 00:07:29,777
Mimi, let me take over the dishes now.

199
00:07:30,027 --> 00:07:31,226
No, that's okay. Hold on.

200
00:07:31,227 --> 00:07:33,587
Go take a shower. Wait, no. That's not what I meant to say.

201
00:07:33,727 --> 00:07:34,797
Am I...

202
00:07:35,097 --> 00:07:36,166
Am I dirty?

203
00:07:36,167 --> 00:07:37,967
(While Mimi is starting to lose her focus...)

204
00:07:38,007 --> 00:07:39,966
- The pasta is good, isn't it?
- Yes, it's tasty.

205
00:07:39,967 --> 00:07:41,477
Right. Everything is good.

206
00:07:41,937 --> 00:07:44,606
Is the entire cast of "Earth Entertainment TV" here?

207
00:07:44,607 --> 00:07:46,523
The whole cast of "Earth Entertainment TV" is here.

208
00:07:46,547 --> 00:07:48,116
- Are all of you here?
- I understood her instantly.

209
00:07:48,117 --> 00:07:50,577
All four of us from "Earth Entertainment TV" are here.

210
00:07:51,887 --> 00:07:53,187
But I don't see Mimi.

211
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:55,416
Mimi is the one who made that pollack roe and clam pasta.

212
00:07:55,417 --> 00:07:56,687
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

213
00:07:57,457 --> 00:07:58,557
Mimi made it.

214
00:07:59,627 --> 00:08:00,656
(She delivers the news right away.)

215
00:08:00,657 --> 00:08:02,756
Mimi, they're really enjoying your pollack roe and clam pasta.

216
00:08:02,757 --> 00:08:03,826
- Really? I'm relieved.
- Yes.

217
00:08:03,827 --> 00:08:06,567
And a customer asked for you. "Where is Mimi?"

218
00:08:07,297 --> 00:08:08,366
- Young Ji.
- Pardon?

219
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:10,367
- I'll go to see this customer.
- Yes, Mimi? Okay.

220
00:08:10,437 --> 00:08:12,007
- Hurry up. She just left.
- Okay.

221
00:08:12,307 --> 00:08:13,937
(Rushing over to say hello)

222
00:08:14,407 --> 00:08:15,437
Hello.

223
00:08:16,007 --> 00:08:17,946
- You're still here. Hello.
- We'll come back.

224
00:08:17,947 --> 00:08:20,746
- Did you enjoy the food?
- I'm a fan of yours.

225
00:08:20,747 --> 00:08:21,776
Oh, really?

226
00:08:21,777 --> 00:08:22,846
(Grateful)

227
00:08:22,847 --> 00:08:24,963
I said my favourite was the pollack roe and clam pasta,

228
00:08:24,987 --> 00:08:26,286
and she said you made it.

229
00:08:26,287 --> 00:08:27,656
(She chuckles while saying, "She said you made it.")

230
00:08:27,657 --> 00:08:28,657
Thank you.

231
00:08:28,987 --> 00:08:31,127
Take care. I'll go back inside.

232
00:08:31,227 --> 00:08:32,957
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye. Go home safely.

233
00:08:33,857 --> 00:08:36,997
(The mini fan event is over.)

234
00:08:37,667 --> 00:08:40,167
(Current Time: 3:30pm)

235
00:08:40,497 --> 00:08:43,037
(10 hours have passed since they came to work.)

236
00:08:43,697 --> 00:08:48,777
(That means it's about time their bodies started aching.)

237
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,276
Give me a second.

238
00:08:50,277 --> 00:08:53,146
(Both the experienced member...)

239
00:08:53,147 --> 00:08:56,617
(and the younger member are getting tired.)

240
00:08:57,277 --> 00:09:00,387
(The sparkle in Yu Jin's eyes has vanished.)

241
00:09:01,557 --> 00:09:05,127
(Mimi's joints are stiff.)

242
00:09:05,987 --> 00:09:10,627
(Everyone is getting tired.)

243
00:09:11,497 --> 00:09:15,297
(Even so, Young Ji gets it together and washes the dishes.)

244
00:09:16,337 --> 00:09:18,836
- A thought just crossed my mind.
- What is it?

245
00:09:18,837 --> 00:09:20,877
Do you think we're paying for our karma right now?

246
00:09:25,307 --> 00:09:26,447
I'm having a great time.

247
00:09:27,377 --> 00:09:29,047
I'm having a great time too.

248
00:09:31,987 --> 00:09:34,186
(Customers rush in again.)

249
00:09:34,187 --> 00:09:37,056
- Hello.
- Hello.

250
00:09:37,057 --> 00:09:38,286
(The service team gets busy again.)

251
00:09:38,287 --> 00:09:40,897
Please take a look and feel free to sit wherever you like.

252
00:09:41,527 --> 00:09:44,397
- Hello.
- Welcome.

253
00:09:44,727 --> 00:09:47,466
- Would you like a bigger table?
- That'd be nice.

254
00:09:47,467 --> 00:09:49,413
All right. I'll get the bigger table ready for you.

255
00:09:49,437 --> 00:09:51,137
(Switching to a 4-seater)

256
00:09:51,367 --> 00:09:52,537
(Shouting gibberish)

257
00:09:53,237 --> 00:09:54,907
I'm bringing in a table. Be careful.

258
00:09:55,477 --> 00:09:57,107
- Princes.
- Hey, move aside.

259
00:09:58,507 --> 00:09:59,907
I just called them "princes."

260
00:10:00,607 --> 00:10:01,927
Then she said, "Hey, move aside."

261
00:10:02,747 --> 00:10:04,546
- Thank you.
- I'll take it out. I'm sorry.

262
00:10:04,547 --> 00:10:07,017
(They finished switching tables.)

263
00:10:07,817 --> 00:10:09,257
Will that be these two dishes, then?

264
00:10:09,657 --> 00:10:11,497
Got it. Let me know if you need anything else.

265
00:10:11,587 --> 00:10:14,397
- And tteokramisu chestnut, please.
- Tteokramisu chestnut.

266
00:10:15,257 --> 00:10:17,867
- We've got a new order in.
- That's great news.

267
00:10:18,297 --> 00:10:21,166
For table 1, 1 original tteokbokki...

268
00:10:21,167 --> 00:10:23,097
and one pollack roe and clam pasta.

269
00:10:23,397 --> 00:10:25,406
A new order for one original tteokbokki.

270
00:10:25,407 --> 00:10:26,567
- A medium size.
- Got it.

271
00:10:26,967 --> 00:10:29,153
- So two medium original tteokbokki?
- It's a new order.

272
00:10:29,177 --> 00:10:30,836
It's a new order from a new table.

273
00:10:30,837 --> 00:10:31,997
- Got it.
- It's a new order.

274
00:10:32,107 --> 00:10:34,647
- Thanks. Cheer up. We've got this!
- We've got this!

275
00:10:35,477 --> 00:10:36,546
Here goes the rice cake.

276
00:10:36,547 --> 00:10:38,387
(She puts garaetteok in for the first order.)

277
00:10:39,047 --> 00:10:41,057
(Mimi checks the temperature of the deep fryer.)

278
00:10:41,787 --> 00:10:43,016
Perfect timing.

279
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:44,427
- Two mediums, right?
- Yes.

280
00:10:45,287 --> 00:10:47,657
(In the kitchen, Mimi prepares deep-fried food.)

281
00:10:48,057 --> 00:10:50,097
(In the hall, Eun Ji serves dongchimi.)

282
00:10:50,457 --> 00:10:51,767
Goodness. I'm so tired.

283
00:10:52,527 --> 00:10:53,567
(Sighing)

284
00:10:53,827 --> 00:10:56,197
This gentleman here says the prices are very low.

285
00:10:56,497 --> 00:10:58,866
This gentleman over here? Thank you so much.

286
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:01,227
- You can charge him more.
- Thank you for your compliment.

287
00:11:01,607 --> 00:11:04,547
(At the same time, Mimi...)

288
00:11:05,047 --> 00:11:09,517
(finished making the deep-fried food for the original tteokbokki.)

289
00:11:09,977 --> 00:11:11,816
(1 pollack roe and clam pasta)

290
00:11:11,817 --> 00:11:14,417
(She moves on to making pollack roe and clam pasta.)

291
00:11:15,057 --> 00:11:17,287
(As she focuses on making the pasta, )

292
00:11:17,887 --> 00:11:21,727
(she has to put in the second batch of deep-fried food.)

293
00:11:24,867 --> 00:11:29,797
(She goes back and forth between the fryer and the stove.)

294
00:11:30,537 --> 00:11:32,407
It's about time for us...

295
00:11:32,867 --> 00:11:33,937
to serve the food.

296
00:11:34,037 --> 00:11:36,277
- It'll be ready in three minutes.
- Okay.

297
00:11:36,977 --> 00:11:39,407
We can serve pollack roe and clam pasta first.

298
00:11:39,807 --> 00:11:40,847
(Chuckling)

299
00:11:41,777 --> 00:11:43,447
(Me?)

300
00:11:44,617 --> 00:11:45,977
This dish takes longer to prepare.

301
00:11:46,117 --> 00:11:47,757
That's the problem.

302
00:11:48,617 --> 00:11:51,157
Once it gets sweet and soft,

303
00:11:51,757 --> 00:11:53,227
you need to, Director,

304
00:11:53,787 --> 00:11:55,396
pour water in the frying pan.

305
00:11:55,397 --> 00:11:56,426
(Mimi: "Pour water in the frying pan.")

306
00:11:56,427 --> 00:11:58,427
We can pour in a little more water.

307
00:11:59,327 --> 00:12:00,996
Add a little bit of chicken stock.

308
00:12:00,997 --> 00:12:03,443
(What she's trying to say is that it takes quite a long time.)

309
00:12:03,467 --> 00:12:04,937
How's everyone doing right now?

310
00:12:05,537 --> 00:12:06,767
I'm fine.

311
00:12:07,637 --> 00:12:08,637
I'm fine.

312
00:12:09,137 --> 00:12:10,237
I love you.

313
00:12:11,077 --> 00:12:12,077
Yes.

314
00:12:12,347 --> 00:12:14,077
(Chuckling)

315
00:12:14,417 --> 00:12:16,017
(Giggling)

316
00:12:16,347 --> 00:12:17,716
Please say you love me.

317
00:12:17,717 --> 00:12:19,246
I love you. I love you so much.

318
00:12:19,247 --> 00:12:21,286
- I love you.
- I love you.

319
00:12:21,287 --> 00:12:22,517
I love you.

320
00:12:23,057 --> 00:12:25,687
- Medium original tteokbokki is up.
- Got it.

321
00:12:26,327 --> 00:12:28,797
How's our pace? We're still a bit slow, right?

322
00:12:29,227 --> 00:12:30,926
- Today is our first day.
- This is fast enough.

323
00:12:30,927 --> 00:12:32,096
- Really? Are we doing okay?
- You're doing well.

324
00:12:32,097 --> 00:12:33,126
(1 medium original tteokbokki)

325
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,227
It's our first day, so...

326
00:12:34,967 --> 00:12:36,847
My original tteokbokki is quite consistent now.

327
00:12:37,537 --> 00:12:40,037
(It's boiled down to perfection.)

328
00:12:40,437 --> 00:12:46,047
(She adds the fried seafood on top of the tteokbokki.)

329
00:12:47,107 --> 00:12:48,847
Young Ji, you're picking up speed. Nice.

330
00:12:49,777 --> 00:12:51,446
- I'm multitasking right now.
- That's great.

331
00:12:51,447 --> 00:12:53,047
- I love you.
- You're picking up speed.

332
00:12:53,117 --> 00:12:55,717
- Eun Ji, I love you.
- I love you too, Young Ji.

333
00:12:56,217 --> 00:12:58,557
(1 medium original tteokbokki)

334
00:12:59,057 --> 00:13:02,126
Yu Jin, let me take over the dishes now.

335
00:13:02,127 --> 00:13:04,257
Okay. Then Young Ji, can you...

336
00:13:05,527 --> 00:13:08,337
Can you put this aside... Is she gone?

337
00:13:08,967 --> 00:13:10,466
(At the same time, Young Ji is...)

338
00:13:10,467 --> 00:13:11,547
(Putting food in her mouth)

339
00:13:11,967 --> 00:13:13,006
Is she gone?

340
00:13:13,007 --> 00:13:15,507
- I'm here. I'm listening.
- Can you put this aside?

341
00:13:15,907 --> 00:13:17,877
(While heading over to help Yu Jin...)

342
00:13:18,177 --> 00:13:19,276
I already washed it.

343
00:13:19,277 --> 00:13:21,147
(Young Ji eats more food.)

344
00:13:21,377 --> 00:13:24,277
- Make some room for this, please.
- Got it.

345
00:13:24,547 --> 00:13:25,586
- Young Ji.
- Yes?

346
00:13:25,587 --> 00:13:27,187
Why did you eat the leftover tteokbokki?

347
00:13:27,987 --> 00:13:28,987
To figure out why they left it.

348
00:13:28,987 --> 00:13:29,987
- Really?
- Yes.

349
00:13:30,357 --> 00:13:32,186
Why didn't they finish it? Was the sausage too salty?

350
00:13:32,187 --> 00:13:33,587
Or was the rice cake...

351
00:13:34,287 --> 00:13:35,297
They left quite a lot.

352
00:13:35,827 --> 00:13:37,897
So I ate some, and I realised...

353
00:13:39,427 --> 00:13:40,427
Honestly, it was good.

354
00:13:40,627 --> 00:13:42,536
I'll reduce the portion size from now on.

355
00:13:42,537 --> 00:13:43,696
(It seems like portion control is needed.)

356
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,183
Just enough to leave them wanting more.

357
00:13:45,207 --> 00:13:47,937
(The pollack roe and clam pasta is ready too.)

358
00:13:48,207 --> 00:13:49,577
(1 pollack roe and clam pasta)

359
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:51,077
The pasta...

360
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:53,607
- is up. Should I serve it?
- Okay.

361
00:13:54,177 --> 00:13:56,376
- Want to try serving it? Go ahead.
- Eun Ji. Shall I?

362
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:57,857
(Mimi is serving the food this time.)

363
00:13:57,917 --> 00:14:00,317
Who ordered pollack roe and clam pasta?

364
00:14:00,687 --> 00:14:02,717
(They find her cute.)

365
00:14:03,317 --> 00:14:06,427
Who ordered pollack roe and clam pasta?

366
00:14:06,657 --> 00:14:08,257
- Here.
- Oh, I see.

367
00:14:08,497 --> 00:14:10,056
- Mimi.
- Hello.

368
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,696
- Hello.
- Oh, thank you, sir.

369
00:14:11,697 --> 00:14:12,897
(1 pollack roe and clam pasta)

370
00:14:12,997 --> 00:14:15,196
I tried my best to make it delicious.

371
00:14:15,197 --> 00:14:16,266
This is Kim Mimi.

372
00:14:16,267 --> 00:14:19,737
Please mix the thing that's on top with that thing...

373
00:14:20,367 --> 00:14:22,436
- Try eating it that way, please.
- Okay. Thank you.

374
00:14:22,437 --> 00:14:24,336
I think she was trying to tell you...

375
00:14:24,337 --> 00:14:26,477
to gently break up and spread the pollack roe.

376
00:14:26,747 --> 00:14:29,417
(She basically provided simultaneous interpretation.)

377
00:14:29,917 --> 00:14:31,246
How are our customers doing?

378
00:14:31,247 --> 00:14:33,186
- Our customers are...
- Are they having a good time?

379
00:14:33,187 --> 00:14:35,286
Yes, they're having a good time. Most of them are families.

380
00:14:35,287 --> 00:14:36,367
Are they enjoying the food?

381
00:14:36,587 --> 00:14:37,687
- Absolutely.
- Really?

382
00:14:38,087 --> 00:14:40,127
Honestly, I felt too rushed to watch them eat.

383
00:14:41,027 --> 00:14:43,027
(Don't worry. We have Eun Ji, the manager.)

384
00:14:43,427 --> 00:14:44,826
- Is it not too spicy for you?
- No.

385
00:14:44,827 --> 00:14:46,587
- No. It's okay.
- For the children as well?

386
00:14:47,227 --> 00:14:50,536
Please let me know when you're ready for dessert.

387
00:14:50,537 --> 00:14:51,606
- Okay.
- Can we have it now?

388
00:14:51,607 --> 00:14:52,637
I'll bring it now.

389
00:14:52,937 --> 00:14:54,537
They're ready for the tteokramisu now.

390
00:14:56,537 --> 00:14:58,147
(It just came out of the fridge?)

391
00:14:58,407 --> 00:15:00,177
(We'll show you how that happened.)

392
00:15:00,747 --> 00:15:02,317
(As soon as they received the order...)

393
00:15:03,477 --> 00:15:04,687
I'll just make it now.

394
00:15:05,587 --> 00:15:08,517
(Being smart, she made the dessert ahead of time.)

395
00:15:10,287 --> 00:15:12,457
(Once the tteokramisu chestnut was ready, )

396
00:15:13,187 --> 00:15:15,927
(she put it in the fridge.)

397
00:15:16,197 --> 00:15:17,927
- I'll do the dishes for a bit.
- Okay.

398
00:15:18,597 --> 00:15:20,997
(She did all of that and even helped with the dishes.)

399
00:15:22,067 --> 00:15:25,336
Do you know Chef Kwon Sung Jun from "Culinary Class Wars?"

400
00:15:25,337 --> 00:15:27,606
- That's his photo over there. Yes.
- Right.

401
00:15:27,607 --> 00:15:30,637
- He's called Neapolitan Matfia.
- I watched the show.

402
00:15:30,737 --> 00:15:32,247
We learned his recipe.

403
00:15:32,777 --> 00:15:34,947
It's a reimagined version of tiramisu.

404
00:15:36,447 --> 00:15:38,917
- Oh, my. It's good.
- It's good.

405
00:15:39,247 --> 00:15:41,556
(Meanwhile, the kitchen is cleared of orders.)

406
00:15:41,557 --> 00:15:43,017
I love you.

407
00:15:44,357 --> 00:15:45,986
- Don't you love me?
- I love you.

408
00:15:45,987 --> 00:15:47,926
If you love me, you must say it back to me.

409
00:15:47,927 --> 00:15:49,257
I love you.

410
00:15:49,957 --> 00:15:51,056
Not yet.

411
00:15:51,057 --> 00:15:52,203
(Dirty plates are coming in instead of love.)

412
00:15:52,227 --> 00:15:54,766
(Dirty plates)

413
00:15:54,767 --> 00:15:55,837
Welcome.

414
00:15:56,367 --> 00:15:57,487
They keep rolling in, right?

415
00:15:57,797 --> 00:16:00,207
- Pass the baton to someone else.
- Okay.

416
00:16:00,637 --> 00:16:03,177
(Even after that, dirty plates keep coming in.)

417
00:16:04,707 --> 00:16:06,447
Coming through.

418
00:16:06,847 --> 00:16:07,877
- What is it?
- Sorry?

419
00:16:08,277 --> 00:16:09,597
- What were you doing?
- Nothing.

420
00:16:10,647 --> 00:16:15,117
(Young Ji's soul is leaving her body.)

421
00:16:16,057 --> 00:16:17,956
How are you all doing? Are you good? I love you.

422
00:16:17,957 --> 00:16:18,957
I love you.

423
00:16:18,958 --> 00:16:19,986
I love you.

424
00:16:19,987 --> 00:16:21,747
(Suddenly, the kitchen is filled with love.)

425
00:16:21,827 --> 00:16:24,457
We must love even when we're dying of exhaustion.

426
00:16:25,697 --> 00:16:26,726
(Seriously...)

427
00:16:26,727 --> 00:16:27,797
You're right.

428
00:16:28,137 --> 00:16:30,967
We must love. We must stick together even when we hate each other.

429
00:16:31,367 --> 00:16:34,607
It's scary how Young Ji has so many different personas.

430
00:16:35,037 --> 00:16:37,397
Sometimes she's like Ms. Ma Bok Rim, the tteokbokki legend.

431
00:16:37,777 --> 00:16:39,137
She's just herself at other times.

432
00:16:39,407 --> 00:16:41,447
- I love you.
- She turns into the head chef too.

433
00:16:42,247 --> 00:16:43,777
(The dishes are done.)

434
00:16:45,387 --> 00:16:49,617
(She walks over to Mimi, clutching her aching joints.)

435
00:16:51,287 --> 00:16:52,787
(Groaning)

436
00:16:53,427 --> 00:16:55,526
(As her back finally stretches, )

437
00:16:55,527 --> 00:16:59,327
(her groans echo through the kitchen.)

438
00:16:59,627 --> 00:17:00,667
Can you do it for me?

439
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:02,496
One, two, three.

440
00:17:02,497 --> 00:17:03,697
(Groaning)

441
00:17:04,537 --> 00:17:05,566
It's beautiful.

442
00:17:05,567 --> 00:17:07,607
(Mimi bounces her knees with Young Ji on her back.)

443
00:17:07,707 --> 00:17:09,837
(Her loud groans echo down the hallway and beyond.)

444
00:17:10,307 --> 00:17:11,947
(Groaning and laughing)

445
00:17:12,477 --> 00:17:14,207
- That's Young Ji's voice.
- Is it?

446
00:17:14,307 --> 00:17:15,747
- She has a loud voice.
- It's okay.

447
00:17:15,777 --> 00:17:18,417
- She's the loudest on the show.
- Yes, she's loud.

448
00:17:19,787 --> 00:17:22,517
Her voice is so loud. It sounded like a street fight from afar.

449
00:17:23,517 --> 00:17:26,277
She's always loud and boisterous. That's why she's called "Loud One."

450
00:17:27,887 --> 00:17:30,827
(She helps Yu Jin stretch her back as well.)

451
00:17:31,367 --> 00:17:33,566
- Okay. You feel better now, right?
- Yes.

452
00:17:33,567 --> 00:17:35,007
- You feel better now, right?
- Yes.

453
00:17:35,037 --> 00:17:36,996
Can you keep checking on the dining area?

454
00:17:36,997 --> 00:17:39,066
- I'll take a look.
- They might be ready to pay.

455
00:17:39,067 --> 00:17:40,367
(Young Ji springs into action.)

456
00:17:40,667 --> 00:17:42,237
Hello, I'm the chef.

457
00:17:42,477 --> 00:17:43,777
Are you enjoying the food?

458
00:17:43,837 --> 00:17:46,076
- I recognise your voice.
- Hello.

459
00:17:46,077 --> 00:17:48,037
Please enjoy your food and have a wonderful time.

460
00:17:48,077 --> 00:17:49,846
Thank you. Sir, you're very handsome.

461
00:17:49,847 --> 00:17:51,367
- Thank you.
- Please enjoy your food.

462
00:17:52,387 --> 00:17:54,117
Hello. Did you just arrive?

463
00:17:54,587 --> 00:17:56,387
You just arrived? Would you like to come in?

464
00:17:56,557 --> 00:17:57,717
Yu Jin, we have customers.

465
00:17:57,787 --> 00:17:59,956
- Hello.
- Yu Jin, we have customers.

466
00:17:59,957 --> 00:18:02,457
Hello, baby. A baby is here. It's a baby.

467
00:18:03,127 --> 00:18:04,157
- A baby is here.
- Hi.

468
00:18:04,197 --> 00:18:06,467
Please sit wherever you'd like.

469
00:18:07,867 --> 00:18:09,766
- Hyun Seok.
- Gosh, aunt.

470
00:18:09,767 --> 00:18:10,966
- Hyun Seok.
- Hello, uncle.

471
00:18:10,967 --> 00:18:12,766
What brings you here? Hello.

472
00:18:12,767 --> 00:18:14,536
What do you mean? We came to eat.

473
00:18:14,537 --> 00:18:16,276
We happened to see this place while passing by.

474
00:18:16,277 --> 00:18:17,536
- Hello.
- Hello.

475
00:18:17,537 --> 00:18:19,347
- Our baby.
- Long time, no see.

476
00:18:19,907 --> 00:18:23,677
(Young Ji gets a baby chair ready first.)

477
00:18:23,917 --> 00:18:25,616
(Passing it to the expert)

478
00:18:25,617 --> 00:18:28,187
- Do you need a baby chair?
- Yes.

479
00:18:28,287 --> 00:18:29,457
Thank you.

480
00:18:29,687 --> 00:18:31,186
I'll help you with the payment.

481
00:18:31,187 --> 00:18:33,003
(She helps with the payment after handing over the chair.)

482
00:18:33,027 --> 00:18:35,257
- Thank you. Please take care.
- Thank you.

483
00:18:36,127 --> 00:18:37,527
Shall we try this one?

484
00:18:37,997 --> 00:18:39,026
- Or that one?
- Won't it be too spicy?

485
00:18:39,027 --> 00:18:40,127
Wait, which one is better?

486
00:18:40,697 --> 00:18:42,566
- Let's try that one.
- Get a small one.

487
00:18:42,567 --> 00:18:43,667
Hi there.

488
00:18:44,267 --> 00:18:45,536
- Come here.
- A small one.

489
00:18:45,537 --> 00:18:47,807
Come to grandma. Come to me.

490
00:18:48,477 --> 00:18:50,557
- He's still shy around strangers.
- I can see that.

491
00:18:50,707 --> 00:18:52,246
- Another order came in.
- Okay.

492
00:18:52,247 --> 00:18:54,046
One small original tteokbokki...

493
00:18:54,047 --> 00:18:55,417
and one chestnut tiramisu.

494
00:18:55,817 --> 00:18:57,246
- What?
- One chestnut tiramisu.

495
00:18:57,247 --> 00:18:58,847
- Chestnut tiramisu?
- Wait.

496
00:18:58,987 --> 00:19:01,317
I should be upset that I didn't get an order.

497
00:19:01,587 --> 00:19:03,686
But I’m just so happy that I get to support Young Ji.

498
00:19:03,687 --> 00:19:05,487
I can focus on supporting her.

499
00:19:05,887 --> 00:19:08,527
(Starting the tteokbokki with some support)

500
00:19:08,857 --> 00:19:11,197
(While waiting for it to cook down, )

501
00:19:11,597 --> 00:19:13,396
(let's watch something cute.)

502
00:19:13,397 --> 00:19:15,467
