587
00:22:06,037 --> 00:22:07,936
They're the spiciest peppers in the world,

588
00:22:07,937 --> 00:22:09,006
and it's an eating challenge.

589
00:22:09,007 --> 00:22:10,437
- My gosh.
- Also known as...

590
00:22:11,077 --> 00:22:13,606
They'll be your last customers, so please do your best.

591
00:22:13,607 --> 00:22:15,946
- Okay.
- We always do our best.

592
00:22:15,947 --> 00:22:17,646
Whether it's the last customer, the first customer,

593
00:22:17,647 --> 00:22:19,316
a customer in the middle of the day, or the seventh customer,

594
00:22:19,317 --> 00:22:22,087
you give it your all. That's the mindset of running your business.

595
00:22:22,257 --> 00:22:24,786
Just because they’re the last customer doesn’t mean...

596
00:22:24,787 --> 00:22:27,087
- Think of it...
- What kind of mindset is that?

597
00:22:27,757 --> 00:22:30,157
- as mala-style tteokbokki.
- The 3rd, 4th, 5th, 6th, 7th...

598
00:22:30,497 --> 00:22:32,097
- Please excuse me for a minute.
- Sure.

599
00:22:32,167 --> 00:22:34,297
Chef, can you be quiet?

600
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:37,737
(A voice that sounds like a serious scolding)

601
00:22:38,867 --> 00:22:41,367
We can hear you very clearly.

602
00:22:41,907 --> 00:22:43,837
You're embarrassing us.

603
00:22:44,577 --> 00:22:46,476
How amateur must we look...

604
00:22:46,477 --> 00:22:48,106
