775
00:28:48,067 --> 00:28:49,437
I'll take a photo.

776
00:28:49,837 --> 00:28:51,353
- One, two, three.
- I can't believe they finished it.

777
00:28:51,377 --> 00:28:52,407
Click.

778
00:28:52,507 --> 00:28:55,517
This is for those who clear the challenge.

779
00:28:56,677 --> 00:28:58,917
Congratulations again.

780
00:28:59,187 --> 00:29:00,246
Thank you.

781
00:29:00,247 --> 00:29:01,686
Thanks to you, it will be spicier...

782
00:29:01,687 --> 00:29:03,656
for those who take on this challenge tomorrow.

783
00:29:03,657 --> 00:29:04,757
It will be much spicier.

784
00:29:05,257 --> 00:29:07,326
Your total is only 29.9 dollars.

785
00:29:07,327 --> 00:29:08,756
(Jade Emperor Tteokbokki is free when you succeed.)

786
00:29:08,757 --> 00:29:10,397
- Aren't you glad that you did it?
- Yes.

787
00:29:10,697 --> 00:29:12,227
We succeeded because it was delicious.

788
00:29:12,527 --> 00:29:15,027
Really? I'll tell everyone in the kitchen.

789
00:29:15,227 --> 00:29:16,496
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

790
00:29:16,497 --> 00:29:17,737
- Please come again.
- Goodbye.

791
00:29:18,637 --> 00:29:20,667
I have plans to make it spicier.

792
00:29:20,937 --> 00:29:22,307
I just went easy on them.

793
00:29:23,137 --> 00:29:26,376
(It's time to close the restaurant.)

794
00:29:26,377 --> 00:29:28,647
(Open for business)

795
00:29:29,647 --> 00:29:34,017
(Closed for business)

796
00:29:34,247 --> 00:29:36,016
- Let's clean up.
- Yes, let's clean up.

797
00:29:36,017 --> 00:29:37,417
(Current Time: 5:52pm)

798
00:29:37,617 --> 00:29:40,357
Gosh, Young Ji should come and look at this.

799
00:29:40,887 --> 00:29:41,986
Young Ji.

800
00:29:41,987 --> 00:29:43,357
- Young Ji, Mimi.
- Yes?

801
00:29:43,527 --> 00:29:45,326
- It's a very beautiful sight.
- It really is.

802
00:29:45,327 --> 00:29:47,167
- Mimi should come too.
- Hey, Mimi.

803
00:29:48,327 --> 00:29:50,436
This is why...

804
00:29:50,437 --> 00:29:51,836
- Young Ji.
- I'm about to cry.

805
00:29:51,837 --> 00:29:52,837
Girls.

806
00:29:53,267 --> 00:29:54,566
- Take a look.
- It's going to make me cry.

807
00:29:54,567 --> 00:29:55,976
They finished all the food.

808
00:29:55,977 --> 00:29:58,806
- So...
- It's really going to make me cry.

809
00:29:58,807 --> 00:30:00,377
This is their response to your cooking.

810
00:30:00,977 --> 00:30:02,976
- It looks delicious.
- They even finished the dongchimi.

811
00:30:02,977 --> 00:30:04,546
This is their response.

812
00:30:04,547 --> 00:30:06,846
- They must've enjoyed it.
- It was very well received.

813
00:30:06,847 --> 00:30:08,916
We couldn't go over it because we were too busy.

814
00:30:08,917 --> 00:30:09,917
You're right.

815
00:30:09,987 --> 00:30:11,456
- This is incredible.
- Eun Ji,

816
00:30:11,457 --> 00:30:13,157
you worked so hard today.

817
00:30:13,757 --> 00:30:15,726
- Well done, everyone.
- Thank you.

818
00:30:15,727 --> 00:30:17,903
Let's give ourselves a round of applause for our hard work.

819
00:30:17,927 --> 00:30:19,043
(Patting herself on the back)

820
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:21,326
- First of all, our two servers...
- Yes.

821
00:30:21,327 --> 00:30:22,936
You two served customers, washed dishes,

822
00:30:22,937 --> 00:30:25,197
made chestnut tiramisu, made slushies,

823
00:30:25,337 --> 00:30:27,806
and even attracted customers in the beginning.

824
00:30:27,807 --> 00:30:28,807
Don't forget the dongchimi.

825
00:30:28,808 --> 00:30:30,106
- Dongchimi.
- You also made dongchimi.

826
00:30:30,107 --> 00:30:31,736
You filmed Reels, became balloon decorations for the event.

827
00:30:31,737 --> 00:30:33,276
You did a bit of everything, helped us out, supported us,

828
00:30:33,277 --> 00:30:34,906
- and took care of us. And...
- We went grocery shopping.

829
00:30:34,907 --> 00:30:35,946
You even went grocery shopping...

830
00:30:35,947 --> 00:30:37,616
in the pouring rain.

831
00:30:37,617 --> 00:30:39,616
You fought through the typhoon and washed dishes.

832
00:30:39,617 --> 00:30:42,417
You managed to keep your composure and your spirits up.

833
00:30:42,857 --> 00:30:44,656
Give yourselves a big round of applause...

834
00:30:44,657 --> 00:30:46,387
for your fair play.

835
00:30:47,527 --> 00:30:49,326
- I really like working with her.
- Next is Kim Mi Hyun.

836
00:30:49,327 --> 00:30:50,526
- She's very smart.
- You washed dishes,

837
00:30:50,527 --> 00:30:52,266
rinsed dishcloths, cut the rice cakes,

838
00:30:52,267 --> 00:30:53,926
made jeolpyeon, became my friend...

839
00:30:53,927 --> 00:30:55,866
and my right-hand woman. You washed dishes,

840
00:30:55,867 --> 00:30:57,436
made pollack roe and clam pasta.

841
00:30:57,437 --> 00:30:59,636
Everyone loves your pollack roe and clam pasta.

842
00:30:59,637 --> 00:31:02,307
Everyone likes your food.

843
00:31:02,607 --> 00:31:04,176
You also made fried food, took it out,

844
00:31:04,177 --> 00:31:06,276
let it dry, cooled it down, and plated it.

845
00:31:06,277 --> 00:31:07,546
You kept me sane,

846
00:31:07,547 --> 00:31:09,223
you set the timer and made sure the timer went off.

847
00:31:09,247 --> 00:31:11,247
- She's perfect.
- Please clap for Mi Hyun.

848
00:31:12,077 --> 00:31:13,086
(It was my pleasure.)

849
00:31:13,087 --> 00:31:14,916
- Well done today.
- You worked the hardest.

850
00:31:14,917 --> 00:31:15,917
Give yourself a compliment too.

851
00:31:15,918 --> 00:31:17,438
- Give yourself a compliment.
- Right.

852
00:31:17,657 --> 00:31:19,226
You made the sauce, prepped ingredients,

853
00:31:19,227 --> 00:31:20,656
- grilled, and did everything.
- You created the challenge.

854
00:31:20,657 --> 00:31:21,657
You came up with the challenge...

855
00:31:21,658 --> 00:31:23,326
and planned everything.

856
00:31:23,327 --> 00:31:24,327
- You're cute.
- You washed dishes,

857
00:31:24,328 --> 00:31:25,666
- assigned everyone their roles, - Right.

858
00:31:25,667 --> 00:31:26,866
And got the aprons ready.

859
00:31:26,867 --> 00:31:29,136
Anyway, well done. I'm glad that we have pockets on our aprons.

860
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:30,566
- Was it uncomfortable?
- No, it's comfortable.

861
00:31:30,567 --> 00:31:32,506
- I really like it.
- Let me know if there's a problem.

862
00:31:32,507 --> 00:31:34,866
- It's the best.
- So today,

863
00:31:34,867 --> 00:31:37,337
- how did we do on sales?
- Today's sales?

864
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:38,437
(Day 1 of business)

865
00:31:38,438 --> 00:31:39,806
(The sales are revealed.)

866
00:31:39,807 --> 00:31:40,847
Get ready.

867
00:31:40,977 --> 00:31:42,106
- Seriously.
- I will announce...

868
00:31:42,107 --> 00:31:43,246
- the sales amount.
- How much did we make?

869
00:31:43,247 --> 00:31:44,647
Let's start with the card reader.

870
00:31:45,377 --> 00:31:47,587
- We earned 296.8 dollars.
- It's about 300 dollars.

871
00:31:47,787 --> 00:31:48,956
When rounded up, it's 300 dollars.

872
00:31:48,957 --> 00:31:50,093
(Self-congratulatory applause)

873
00:31:50,117 --> 00:31:52,237
- That's only from the card reader.
- How about cash?

874
00:31:52,457 --> 00:31:53,527
How about cash?

875
00:31:54,657 --> 00:31:55,657
Oh, my.

876
00:31:56,157 --> 00:31:57,996
- We earned 300 dollars.
- The total is 400 dollars.

877
00:31:57,997 --> 00:31:59,366
We earned close to 400 dollars.

878
00:31:59,367 --> 00:32:00,827
It's about 390 dollars.

879
00:32:00,967 --> 00:32:02,566
(4 small original tteokbokki, 6 medium original tteokbokki, )

880
00:32:02,567 --> 00:32:04,196
(3 ghost pepper mala tteokbokki, 1 Jade Emperor Tteokbokki...)

881
00:32:04,197 --> 00:32:06,036
(Minus 11.5 dollars due to Yu Jin's mistake)

882
00:32:06,037 --> 00:32:07,666
(Total sales: 327.8 dollars)

883
00:32:07,667 --> 00:32:09,076
- We earned a lot.
- How did we make so much?

884
00:32:09,077 --> 00:32:10,177
Let's clap for each other.

885
00:32:10,907 --> 00:32:12,177
It's a big success today.

886
00:32:12,847 --> 00:32:14,367
- Seriously...
- Let's hug each other.

887
00:32:15,047 --> 00:32:16,977
- Hug me.
- We'll be busier tomorrow.

888
00:32:17,217 --> 00:32:19,086
When I say "honesty," please say "humility."

889
00:32:19,087 --> 00:32:20,586
- Honesty.
- Humility.

890
00:32:20,587 --> 00:32:21,746
- Ahk.
- Ahk.

891
00:32:21,747 --> 00:32:24,017
You guys are the best.

892
00:32:24,217 --> 00:32:27,026
Let's wrap things up and buy some at the supermarket.

893
00:32:27,027 --> 00:32:29,126
- I'd be so grateful.
- Buy it at the supermarket.

894
00:32:29,127 --> 00:32:30,127
Anything sounds good.

895
00:32:30,127 --> 00:32:31,127
Let's grill it here...

896
00:32:31,128 --> 00:32:32,397
and enjoy it with tteokbokki.

897
00:32:33,097 --> 00:32:34,426
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you.

898
00:32:34,427 --> 00:32:36,166
- Bon appetit.
- It's mostly uncooked,

899
00:32:36,167 --> 00:32:37,636
- so take care of it yourself.
- Okay.

900
00:32:37,637 --> 00:32:38,796
No problem.

901
00:32:38,797 --> 00:32:40,937
Well done, everyone.

902
00:32:44,177 --> 00:32:45,907
We bought some really good meat.

903
00:32:48,677 --> 00:32:49,677
(Exclaiming)

904
00:32:49,678 --> 00:32:50,777
The meat is excellent.

905
00:32:51,277 --> 00:32:52,317
Help yourself.

906
00:32:55,247 --> 00:32:56,456
Aren't you glad that we're eating meat?

907
00:32:56,457 --> 00:32:58,256
Once we wash the rice, are we done for today?

908
00:32:58,257 --> 00:32:59,833
- You guys can go home first.
- Unbelievable.

909
00:32:59,857 --> 00:33:01,217
We still have to make basil pesto.

910
00:33:01,427 --> 00:33:03,356
- We have to try it.
- You're right.

911
00:33:03,357 --> 00:33:04,456
We need to taste it.

912
00:33:04,457 --> 00:33:07,097
(Next is tasting the new basil tteokbokki.)

913
00:33:07,367 --> 00:33:09,037
I'm telling you, we're amazing.

914
00:33:09,567 --> 00:33:11,336
We prep, we run the restaurant,

915
00:33:11,337 --> 00:33:12,857
and we do more research after closing.

916
00:33:13,667 --> 00:33:15,037
We even make our own rice cakes.

917
00:33:15,407 --> 00:33:17,037
We're seriously amazing.

918
00:33:17,507 --> 00:33:20,106
What worries me is that basil is tricky.

919
00:33:20,107 --> 00:33:22,083
Once people get a taste of it, all of them want it.

920
00:33:22,107 --> 00:33:24,387
Young Ji isn't very experienced with making basil dishes.

921
00:33:24,917 --> 00:33:26,516
- It's not something...
- You never tried it at home.

922
00:33:26,517 --> 00:33:28,287
- you can practice with at home.
- Right.

923
00:33:28,887 --> 00:33:31,887
You've definitely been showing your INFP side more lately.

924
00:33:32,287 --> 00:33:33,886
- Really?
- I used to question it.

925
00:33:33,887 --> 00:33:35,326
"Is she really an INFP?"

926
00:33:35,327 --> 00:33:37,127
- But lately...
- In what way?

927
00:33:37,597 --> 00:33:39,477
The way you've been feeling overwhelmed lately.

928
00:33:39,967 --> 00:33:41,327
Or is it because of the situation?

929
00:33:41,667 --> 00:33:42,737
Right.

930
00:33:43,167 --> 00:33:45,413
Or maybe I'm starting to understand what you're thinking.

931
00:33:45,437 --> 00:33:47,406
- Maybe you were like this before.
- That's possible.

932
00:33:47,407 --> 00:33:49,653
You never used to show it, but now you're letting it show.

933
00:33:49,677 --> 00:33:51,077
You mean, how I worry about things?

934
00:33:51,637 --> 00:33:53,107
- Your worries...
- Yes.

935
00:33:54,007 --> 00:33:56,217
- and your tender heart.
- My tender heart?

936
00:33:56,447 --> 00:33:58,516
Should you tell me that you love me or not?

937
00:33:58,517 --> 00:33:59,617
I shouldn't.

938
00:33:59,817 --> 00:34:01,287
I say I love you when I do.

939
00:34:01,517 --> 00:34:03,556
- But I don't love you now.
- Do you say it when you love me?

940
00:34:03,557 --> 00:34:05,487
Of course. I'm very sincere about it.

941
00:34:07,027 --> 00:34:08,257
That's even funnier.

942
00:34:08,757 --> 00:34:11,196
There was a moment of absolute rage...

943
00:34:11,197 --> 00:34:13,467
when she was making an ex-boyfriend toast.

944
00:34:13,997 --> 00:34:16,866
"It's my first time running a business too!"

945
00:34:16,867 --> 00:34:18,947
- She said that earlier.
- It's how Young Ji looked.

946
00:34:19,007 --> 00:34:20,867
- When?
- When you were cutting jeolpyeon.

947
00:34:21,107 --> 00:34:22,376
- Mimi looked...
- Was she being serious?

948
00:34:22,377 --> 00:34:25,077
Like a psychopath when she was just slicing the jeolpyeon.

949
00:34:25,277 --> 00:34:27,306
Can I honestly give my one-line review of Mimi?

950
00:34:27,307 --> 00:34:28,647
She's an independence activist.

951
00:34:28,677 --> 00:34:29,746
(It means that she's that strong and unshakable.)

952
00:34:29,747 --> 00:34:31,877
- That's what I think.
- This is all we could hear.

953
00:34:33,447 --> 00:34:35,286
- We didn't even have customers.
- Exactly.

954
00:34:35,287 --> 00:34:36,593
(Walking the long road of jeolpyeon single-handedly)

955
00:34:36,617 --> 00:34:37,787
All of us are...

956
00:34:38,387 --> 00:34:40,107
- unusual.
- Shall I make basil tteokbokki?

957
00:34:40,187 --> 00:34:41,786
What?

958
00:34:41,787 --> 00:34:43,507
- I didn't hear you.
- I'll go and make it.

959
00:34:44,097 --> 00:34:45,896
- We'll go with you.
- Hold on, Young Ji.

960
00:34:45,897 --> 00:34:47,066
- I mean...
- Let's do it together.

961
00:34:47,067 --> 00:34:48,126
It's because...

962
00:34:48,127 --> 00:34:49,597
(It's time for basil.)

963
00:34:49,737 --> 00:34:51,577
- Where's the strainer?
- It's on top of this.

964
00:34:52,137 --> 00:34:53,407
Eun Ji, did you measure 15kg?

965
00:34:53,837 --> 00:34:55,136
I'll make three at the same time.

966
00:34:55,137 --> 00:34:56,336
(The kitchen team tests the new dish.)

967
00:34:56,337 --> 00:34:57,376
I'll start.

968
00:34:57,377 --> 00:34:59,447
(The kitchen team tests the new dish.)

969
00:34:59,677 --> 00:35:01,907
The whole black pepper was there, wasn't it?

970
00:35:02,777 --> 00:35:05,916
(The happy break is too short.)

971
00:35:05,917 --> 00:35:07,386
Do you want to go over there?

972
00:35:07,387 --> 00:35:08,946
There isn't enough space here.

973
00:35:08,947 --> 00:35:12,017
(But the working hours are long.)

974
00:35:12,187 --> 00:35:13,556
I guess the balance is off.

975
00:35:13,557 --> 00:35:15,277
(Two hands that never get a chance to rest)

976
00:35:15,357 --> 00:35:16,496
One, two, three.

977
00:35:16,497 --> 00:35:19,027
(It gets heavier by the day.)

978
00:35:19,227 --> 00:35:20,666
(They finish soaking the rice again today.)

979
00:35:20,667 --> 00:35:21,697
It's done.

980
00:35:23,697 --> 00:35:25,467
- An Yu Genius.
- Yes?

981
00:35:25,537 --> 00:35:27,137
Please chop a lot of green onions today.

982
00:35:27,237 --> 00:35:28,806
I was going to do that tomorrow.

983
00:35:28,807 --> 00:35:30,806
- I'll chop a lot tomorrow.
- I'm sorry.

984
00:35:30,807 --> 00:35:32,407
(Laughing)

985
00:35:33,047 --> 00:35:34,146
You want me to chop them?

986
00:35:34,147 --> 00:35:36,147
(Stop)

987
00:35:36,517 --> 00:35:37,837
- This is the basil sauce?
- Yes.

988
00:35:38,247 --> 00:35:40,086
We still don't have a ladle yet.

989
00:35:40,087 --> 00:35:42,007
I'm a bit nervous. It's my first time trying it.

990
00:35:42,047 --> 00:35:44,217
(Tomorrow's new dish has Eun Ji feeling nervous.)

991
00:35:45,287 --> 00:35:46,887
Broccolino Basiliano.

992
00:35:47,527 --> 00:35:49,396
This looks delicious.

993
00:35:49,397 --> 00:35:51,037
(She pulls out a huge storage container.)

994
00:35:51,157 --> 00:35:53,157
I can tell by looking at the sauce. What do we do?

995
00:35:53,227 --> 00:35:54,667
Can we try some?

996
00:35:54,827 --> 00:35:55,867
Here I go.

997
00:35:56,067 --> 00:35:57,167
Six cups.

998
00:35:57,497 --> 00:35:59,167
Nine cloves of garlic.

999
00:35:59,267 --> 00:36:00,406
Pine nuts.

1000
00:36:00,407 --> 00:36:02,137
One more cup of Parmigiano Reggiano cheese.

1001
00:36:02,367 --> 00:36:03,836
(Young Ji made it earlier.)

1002
00:36:03,837 --> 00:36:04,877
That's great.

1003
00:36:06,007 --> 00:36:08,707
Eun Ji, I'll start cooking it.

1004
00:36:09,947 --> 00:36:11,177
This feels promising.

1005
00:36:11,447 --> 00:36:12,687
Nice.

1006
00:36:13,687 --> 00:36:14,717
I'm glad.

1007
00:36:15,287 --> 00:36:16,517
Thank you.

1008
00:36:16,887 --> 00:36:18,816
Gosh, it smells insanely good.

1009
00:36:18,817 --> 00:36:20,526
- This is delicious.
- Try to find...

1010
00:36:20,527 --> 00:36:22,503
- which side feels easier for you.
- This is very good.

1011
00:36:22,527 --> 00:36:23,857
I'll decorate the dish.

1012
00:36:24,127 --> 00:36:26,066
Yes, start with the broccoli.

1013
00:36:26,067 --> 00:36:27,397
(Fried broccoli)

1014
00:36:27,527 --> 00:36:28,827
(Tater tots)

1015
00:36:28,897 --> 00:36:30,267
(Sun-dried tomatoes)

1016
00:36:30,797 --> 00:36:31,837
Isn't it pretty?

1017
00:36:31,997 --> 00:36:34,007
I should buy one of these too.

1018
00:36:34,067 --> 00:36:35,106
The colours...

1019
00:36:35,107 --> 00:36:37,807
Basil tteokbokki is ready.

1020
00:36:38,037 --> 00:36:39,146
- It's my first time trying it.
- Me too.

1021
00:36:39,147 --> 00:36:40,506
I'd appreciate it if you could give me...

1022
00:36:40,507 --> 00:36:41,606
- your honest opinion.
- It's really my first time.

1023
00:36:41,607 --> 00:36:42,976
Thank you for the food.

1024
00:36:42,977 --> 00:36:44,817
Make sure to try some fried broccoli too.

1025
00:36:45,517 --> 00:36:47,947
(Suddenly tense)

1026
00:36:48,387 --> 00:36:50,087
(Nodding)

1027
00:36:50,257 --> 00:36:51,687
(Humming in approval)

1028
00:36:51,857 --> 00:36:53,337
- I like it.
- I'm glad to hear that.

1029
00:36:53,727 --> 00:36:55,897
It'd be perfect with the original tteokbokki.

1030
00:36:56,457 --> 00:36:57,926
- We can alternate between the two.
- That'd be amazing.

1031
00:36:57,927 --> 00:36:59,027
I have a suggestion.

1032
00:36:59,397 --> 00:37:00,666
I won't be here tomorrow,

1033
00:37:00,667 --> 00:37:02,507
but what do you think about adding bacon here?

1034
00:37:03,297 --> 00:37:04,997
That's a cheat code, but...

1035
00:37:05,097 --> 00:37:06,883
If it's too much extra work, there's no need.

1036
00:37:06,907 --> 00:37:10,007
Basil tteokbokki is already the most labour-intensive one to make.

1037
00:37:10,107 --> 00:37:12,376
Don't you normally make it with sausage?

1038
00:37:12,377 --> 00:37:14,206
- I forgot about the sausage.
- There's sausage in it.

1039
00:37:14,207 --> 00:37:15,346
- In that case...
- There's sausage.

1040
00:37:15,347 --> 00:37:16,976
- There's sausage in it.
- I'll add sausage to it.

1041
00:37:16,977 --> 00:37:18,117
I have another opinion.

1042
00:37:18,677 --> 00:37:20,546
- It's good.
- I can't eat a lot of greasy food.

1043
00:37:20,547 --> 00:37:21,586
- Right.
- I know.

1044
00:37:21,587 --> 00:37:23,987
Should we try sprinkling some black pepper on it?

1045
00:37:24,087 --> 00:37:25,256
- Let's try that.
- Black pepper?

1046
00:37:25,257 --> 00:37:27,386
I said that it had a strong creamy flavour.

1047
00:37:27,387 --> 00:37:29,797
This has less basil flavour than the original.

1048
00:37:29,857 --> 00:37:31,426
I'll add a little more of that tomorrow.

1049
00:37:31,427 --> 00:37:33,096
- If you fix that, it'd be perfect.
- Do you want to practice it now?

1050
00:37:33,097 --> 00:37:34,097
Sure.

1051
00:37:34,098 --> 00:37:35,273
- No, I wasn't serious.
- What?

1052
00:37:35,297 --> 00:37:36,396
(That's enough now.)

1053
00:37:36,397 --> 00:37:37,896
- We have to go home together, - Shall I do it now?

1054
00:37:37,897 --> 00:37:39,206
- No.
- don't we?

1055
00:37:39,207 --> 00:37:40,607
(Current Time: 10:40pm)

1056
00:37:40,807 --> 00:37:42,336
- Honesty.
- Humility.

1057
00:37:42,337 --> 00:37:44,907
- Ahk.
- Ahk. I love you.

1058
00:37:45,577 --> 00:37:46,577
Let's go.

1059
00:37:47,447 --> 00:37:49,007
- Take everything with you.
- Let's go.

1060
00:37:51,447 --> 00:37:53,546
Get some rest. Sleep well.

1061
00:37:53,547 --> 00:37:56,457
(After a long, exhausting day)

1062
00:37:56,817 --> 00:37:58,056
Have a good night.

1063
00:37:58,057 --> 00:37:59,327
(It's time to get some rest.)

1064
00:37:59,587 --> 00:38:02,497
I can't help worrying about the restaurant.

1065
00:38:03,127 --> 00:38:05,126
Here's what I'm worried about.

1066
00:38:05,127 --> 00:38:07,196
- Did you lock the door properly?
- I did.

1067
00:38:07,197 --> 00:38:08,566
What if someone breaks in...

1068
00:38:08,567 --> 00:38:09,936
- and steals the basil pesto?
- I know.

1069
00:38:09,937 --> 00:38:12,196
If they steal our dongchimi, they're done for.

1070
00:38:12,197 --> 00:38:14,007
- Did someone break in?
- Hold on.

1071
00:38:14,107 --> 00:38:15,136
You got an alert.

1072
00:38:15,137 --> 00:38:18,277
"A door opening has been detected. Check the recorded footage?"

1073
00:38:19,347 --> 00:38:21,006
- Hey.
- My goodness.

1074
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:22,376
(The footage is sent to Earth Arcaders in real time.)

1075
00:38:22,377 --> 00:38:23,753
- Who is it?
- But I locked the door.

1076
00:38:23,777 --> 00:38:26,987
(The silhouette looks very familiar.)

1077
00:38:27,287 --> 00:38:29,163
- It's live footage.
- Is it Director Yeong Seok?

1078
00:38:29,187 --> 00:38:30,417
- What?
- Isn't it Yeong Seok?

1079
00:38:30,687 --> 00:38:31,756
It's his bucket hat.

1080
00:38:31,757 --> 00:38:34,257
With that unmistakable middle-aged man vibe,

1081
00:38:34,357 --> 00:38:35,786
it's definitely Yeong Seok.

1082
00:38:35,787 --> 00:38:38,426
What's amazing is that it's nighttime,

1083
00:38:38,427 --> 00:38:39,626
- Right.
- but you can see it clearly.

1084
00:38:39,627 --> 00:38:42,267
- There's no glare or anything.
- You're right.

1085
00:38:42,367 --> 00:38:45,966
I went into the app earlier and turned on security mode.

1086
00:38:45,967 --> 00:38:47,036
(Simply set it up after closing for the day)

1087
00:38:47,037 --> 00:38:49,836
As soon as movement was detected, I got an alert.

1088
00:38:49,837 --> 00:38:51,306
- It's reassuring.
- What is it called?

1089
00:38:51,307 --> 00:38:52,776
- Let's get some rest.
- Let's go to bed.

1090
00:38:52,777 --> 00:38:54,346
- Thank you for your hard work.
- We'll hassle Yeong Seok tomorrow.

1091
00:38:54,347 --> 00:38:55,987
- Good job, everyone.
- See you tomorrow.

1092
00:38:56,077 --> 00:38:57,716
(Young Ji and Yu Jin's room)

1093
00:38:57,717 --> 00:38:59,687
Yu Jin, how was business today?

1094
00:39:00,047 --> 00:39:01,847
Today? I thought...

1095
00:39:02,247 --> 00:39:04,617
(The head chef wants to know how her employee feels.)

1096
00:39:05,087 --> 00:39:08,227
When I first met the elderly customers, it was a little hard.

1097
00:39:08,527 --> 00:39:09,597
To interact with them?

1098
00:39:09,727 --> 00:39:12,597
I struggled with how to keep things flowing naturally.

1099
00:39:13,027 --> 00:39:14,797
Meeting elderly customers was...

1100
00:39:15,597 --> 00:39:18,267
a little challenging, but things got better after that.

1101
00:39:19,067 --> 00:39:20,737
Today was better than I expected.

1102
00:39:20,837 --> 00:39:22,706
It looked like you were having a hard time today.

1103
00:39:22,707 --> 00:39:25,677
- I thought I was going to lose it.
- I know. You struggled a lot.

1104
00:39:26,747 --> 00:39:27,877
Was I being sensitive?

1105
00:39:28,507 --> 00:39:30,276
No, you just looked exhausted.

1106
00:39:30,277 --> 00:39:32,717
I could tell that you were overwhelmed.

1107
00:39:33,687 --> 00:39:36,887
Normally, I'm not...

1108
00:39:37,257 --> 00:39:39,156
- Calm?
- a meticulous person.

1109
00:39:39,157 --> 00:39:40,657
- I see.
- That's what makes it hard.

1110
00:39:40,827 --> 00:39:43,527
(And so, a moment of self-reflection began.)

1111
00:39:43,857 --> 00:39:46,596
I really hate seeing myself when I'm anxious.

1112
00:39:46,597 --> 00:39:47,826
(Young Ji's problem: Being an anxious head chef)

1113
00:39:47,827 --> 00:39:49,737
- I understand how you feel.
- Right?

1114
00:39:50,437 --> 00:39:51,437
Here's how...

1115
00:39:51,797 --> 00:39:54,406
I noticed that you were anxious.

1116
00:39:54,407 --> 00:39:56,276
- You asked 50 questions.
- I did?

1117
00:39:56,277 --> 00:39:58,576
"Should I stop it now? Should I take it out?"

1118
00:39:58,577 --> 00:40:00,776
"Can I take it out directly? Should I stop doing it?"

1119
00:40:00,777 --> 00:40:02,677
"Should I put this back in?"

1120
00:40:02,877 --> 00:40:04,176
You wanted to check everything...

1121
00:40:04,177 --> 00:40:05,476
- that you were doing.
- Right.

1122
00:40:05,477 --> 00:40:06,686
To know if it was right or wrong.

1123
00:40:06,687 --> 00:40:08,163
- I couldn't trust myself.
- Exactly.

1124
00:40:08,187 --> 00:40:09,987
Yu Jin, what's your biggest concern?

1125
00:40:10,387 --> 00:40:12,356
What I'm worried about is...

1126
00:40:12,357 --> 00:40:15,027
- calculating the bills.
- That must be so hard.

1127
00:40:15,287 --> 00:40:16,927
It's harder than you think.

1128
00:40:17,257 --> 00:40:18,956
My hands were shaking...

1129
00:40:18,957 --> 00:40:20,717
with customers waiting right in front of me.

1130
00:40:20,967 --> 00:40:22,066
Earlier today,

1131
00:40:22,067 --> 00:40:23,137
you and your jeolpyeon...

1132
00:40:23,897 --> 00:40:26,466
I thought that you were possessed...

1133
00:40:26,467 --> 00:40:27,707
by a spirit.

1134
00:40:27,937 --> 00:40:30,436
(The older girls are also talking about what happened.)

1135
00:40:30,437 --> 00:40:31,807
You weren't listening.

1136
00:40:32,077 --> 00:40:33,807
You didn't answer when we called you.

1137
00:40:34,807 --> 00:40:36,046
It was so scary.

1138
00:40:36,047 --> 00:40:37,293
(Mimi's problem: Her obsession over jeolpyeon)

1139
00:40:37,317 --> 00:40:40,187
You can't help but fixate on something.

1140
00:40:40,687 --> 00:40:42,407
Mimi, what time are we getting up tomorrow?

1141
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:45,587
- At 6:30am.
- Why so early?

1142
00:40:47,127 --> 00:40:49,926
It's great to run a restaurant with you girls.

1143
00:40:49,927 --> 00:40:50,996
(Hopefully, things will go smoothly tomorrow.)

1144
00:40:50,997 --> 00:40:52,027
I agree.

1145
00:40:54,397 --> 00:40:56,797
(It's the morning of their 2nd day of business.)

1146
00:40:57,597 --> 00:40:59,766
(As if it never rained, )

1147
00:40:59,767 --> 00:41:01,567
(the sunshine is pouring down.)

1148
00:41:02,467 --> 00:41:06,407
(A bright, sunny morning brought the village back to life.)

1149
00:41:07,447 --> 00:41:10,277
(What will Space Rice Cake look like today?)

1150
00:41:12,347 --> 00:41:14,047
(Current Time: 6:20am)

1151
00:41:15,447 --> 00:41:17,317
(The first one to arrive at work is Mimi.)

1152
00:41:18,057 --> 00:41:19,117
Come out.

1153
00:41:20,127 --> 00:41:21,227
What's wrong with my voice?

1154
00:41:23,297 --> 00:41:24,727
Hello. What's that?

1155
00:41:25,397 --> 00:41:27,367
This is the headscarf Eun Ji bought for me.

1156
00:41:28,197 --> 00:41:30,767
(She looks like she's ready to join a hiking club.)

1157
00:41:31,267 --> 00:41:33,427
I was seriously in denial when I woke up this morning.

1158
00:41:34,107 --> 00:41:35,537
Is it 6am already?

1159
00:41:36,637 --> 00:41:37,676
Is it really 6am?

1160
00:41:37,677 --> 00:41:38,853
(Going back to work only about 7 hours later)

1161
00:41:38,877 --> 00:41:41,246
It's cold in the morning and evening here.

1162
00:41:41,247 --> 00:41:43,147
- I know.
- Will we get customers today?

1163
00:41:43,877 --> 00:41:46,016
- If it isn't cold like now...
- Right.

1164
00:41:46,017 --> 00:41:47,987
They'll like outdoors more.

1165
00:41:48,787 --> 00:41:50,616
- Hello.
- Hello.

1166
00:41:50,617 --> 00:41:51,857
Hello.

1167
00:41:52,317 --> 00:41:54,557
We make tteokbokki.

1168
00:41:54,957 --> 00:41:56,697
- Hello.
- Please come and try it.

1169
00:41:57,157 --> 00:41:59,666
- Where is it?
- We'll make tteokbokki there.

1170
00:41:59,667 --> 00:42:01,296
- It's called Space Rice Cake.
- In front of a raw fish restaurant.

1171
00:42:01,297 --> 00:42:03,267
- Okay.
- Thank you.

1172
00:42:04,137 --> 00:42:06,167
- What are the two doing?
- They're coming.

1173
00:42:07,207 --> 00:42:09,977
- The kitchen team seems impatient.
- I know.

1174
00:42:10,277 --> 00:42:11,336
They're always...

1175
00:42:11,337 --> 00:42:12,906
- Could you go first?
- Okay.

1176
00:42:12,907 --> 00:42:14,153
(The impatient kitchen team gets the signboard out.)

1177
00:42:14,177 --> 00:42:15,246
Okay.

1178
00:42:15,247 --> 00:42:16,893
(On the 2nd day of business, they're ready to go.)

1179
00:42:16,917 --> 00:42:19,786
- Honesty. Ahk.
- Humility. Ahk.

1180
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:20,917
Put on your apron.

1181
00:42:21,987 --> 00:42:24,416
- We can do it.
- Let's go.

1182
00:42:24,417 --> 00:42:25,657
I love you all.

1183
00:42:26,057 --> 00:42:28,027
- Shall we get started?
- Yes.

1184
00:42:28,787 --> 00:42:30,056
- Shall I put the strainer on top?
- Yes.

1185
00:42:30,057 --> 00:42:31,497
(Rice that they soaked yesterday)

1186
00:42:31,757 --> 00:42:35,027
We soaked 15kg yesterday. We should weigh it again though.

1187
00:42:35,697 --> 00:42:37,867
The thought of lifting it makes me nervous.

1188
00:42:38,697 --> 00:42:39,743
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

1189
00:42:39,767 --> 00:42:41,967
(Starting with hard physical work early in the morning)

1190
00:42:42,507 --> 00:42:43,937
(Grunting)

1191
00:42:44,337 --> 00:42:46,177
(A rice flour team drowning in cries of agony)

1192
00:42:46,407 --> 00:42:48,446
Are you all right?

1193
00:42:48,447 --> 00:42:49,517
We're okay.

1194
00:42:50,717 --> 00:42:52,547
- It's so heavy.
- The weight is...

1195
00:42:53,087 --> 00:42:54,317
It's 19kg.

1196
00:42:55,317 --> 00:42:57,956
- It absorbed a lot.
- It absorbed a lot of water.

1197
00:42:57,957 --> 00:43:00,403
(It bulked up by 4kg overnight from soaking up all that water.)

1198
00:43:00,427 --> 00:43:01,587
(Shouting)

1199
00:43:02,727 --> 00:43:04,887
(Thankfully, they get their morning strength workout.)

1200
00:43:06,467 --> 00:43:08,467
- Stay strong.
- You can do it.

1201
00:43:09,297 --> 00:43:10,467
It's really heavy.

1202
00:43:10,797 --> 00:43:12,677
(There's nothing easy about making rice cakes.)

1203
00:43:12,907 --> 00:43:13,967
Oh, my.

1204
00:43:14,067 --> 00:43:17,107
We can pull it off if we put our mind to it.

1205
00:43:17,277 --> 00:43:19,847
This is very heavy. It'll be over soon, Eun Ji.

1206
00:43:20,907 --> 00:43:24,017
What happened to the photo studio of us making rice cakes?

1207
00:43:24,377 --> 00:43:25,917
- I'll take photos of you.
- Okay.

1208
00:43:26,347 --> 00:43:29,247
- Looking as tired as possible...
- Get both of us in the frame.

1209
00:43:29,617 --> 00:43:30,956
- Like this... I'll stay low.
- Looking worn out...

1210
00:43:30,957 --> 00:43:33,657
- One, two, three.
- Should I look at the camera?

1211
00:43:34,957 --> 00:43:36,057
Make it look more gruelling.

1212
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:38,297
- Without looking at the camera?
- What?

1213
00:43:38,657 --> 00:43:39,726
Face the camera...

1214
00:43:39,727 --> 00:43:42,227
but stay focused on work.

1215
00:43:42,997 --> 00:43:45,467
(A staged shot made with the photographer’s soul)

1216
00:43:45,997 --> 00:43:47,917
A look that says, "Our rice cakes are the best."

1217
00:43:48,267 --> 00:43:49,606
"It's delicious."

1218
00:43:49,607 --> 00:43:51,277
- Thank you.
- It's done.

1219
00:43:52,707 --> 00:43:53,776
(They're back to work after the photo shoot.)

1220
00:43:53,777 --> 00:43:55,247
My back is about to give out.

1221
00:43:55,477 --> 00:43:57,817
(Mixing away)

1222
00:43:58,647 --> 00:43:59,716
(They even brought in the latest technology, a blender.)

1223
00:43:59,717 --> 00:44:01,217
We're using some modern technology.

1224
00:44:02,117 --> 00:44:04,077
Is there any certification for making tteokbokki?

1225
00:44:04,757 --> 00:44:07,687
- Or making rice cakes.
- We can get certified now.

1226
00:44:08,487 --> 00:44:11,097
- All right!
- You're amazing.

1227
00:44:11,657 --> 00:44:13,596
Rice flour is an impressive thing.

1228
00:44:13,597 --> 00:44:15,027
(Rice flour is getting piled up.)

1229
00:44:15,397 --> 00:44:17,966
- Flour is everything.
- It turned out perfect.

1230
00:44:17,967 --> 00:44:19,713
(Once the finely ground rice flour is transferred into the steamer)

1231
00:44:19,737 --> 00:44:22,537
- Rice flour is ready.
- Way to go.

1232
00:44:23,577 --> 00:44:25,707
(Turning on the steamer at the right time)

1233
00:44:26,277 --> 00:44:27,477
Here it comes.

1234
00:44:29,007 --> 00:44:31,447
It takes some time. It'll be ready in 20 minutes.

1235
00:44:31,677 --> 00:44:33,187
It's hot, so be careful.

1236
00:44:33,447 --> 00:44:35,216
Making rice cakes is no easy job.

1237
00:44:35,217 --> 00:44:37,063
(When covered with a cloth, baekseolgi gets ready.)

1238
00:44:37,087 --> 00:44:39,487
Nice. You're doing so well.

1239
00:44:40,257 --> 00:44:41,817
Mimi, I assembled the rice cake shaper.

1240
00:44:42,227 --> 00:44:44,127
Young Ji, you know exactly what to do now.

1241
00:44:44,857 --> 00:44:47,897
- Mi Hyun, let's make rice cakes.
- Yes, let's go.

1242
00:44:48,767 --> 00:44:50,837
(After steaming it thoroughly)

1243
00:44:51,437 --> 00:44:53,507
- Are we starting with jeolpyeon?
- Yes.

1244
00:44:54,507 --> 00:44:56,183
(Putting baekseolgi into the rice cake shaper)

1245
00:44:56,207 --> 00:44:57,577
It smells so good today.

1246
00:44:58,237 --> 00:45:00,877
- The rice cakes look good today.
- I agree.

1247
00:45:02,147 --> 00:45:03,277
It smells good too.

1248
00:45:03,977 --> 00:45:05,417
(Nervous)

1249
00:45:06,317 --> 00:45:08,517
- Today's rice cakes are the best.
- Are they the best?

1250
00:45:09,017 --> 00:45:10,357
(Yu Jin also takes a bite.)

1251
00:45:10,557 --> 00:45:11,917
Gosh, Eun Ji.

1252
00:45:12,787 --> 00:45:14,587
It tastes like something you'd buy at a shop.

1253
00:45:15,457 --> 00:45:16,926
I'll pull it out,

1254
00:45:16,927 --> 00:45:18,426
- so could you put it in?
- I'll push it in.

1255
00:45:18,427 --> 00:45:20,467
